WHY THIS IS NOT A COPY OF THE APPLICATION'S NOTICE

The desktop application's NOTICE names Pyodide (MPL-2.0, bundled for the sandboxed Python tier),
and records that CUDA, model weights and research papers are deliberately NOT redistributed. It
also points at `resources/licenses/` inside the packaged build and at two CycloneDX SBOMs attached
to each release.

None of that pertains to this website, which ships none of those things and has no packaged build.
Apache-2.0 section 4(d) requires a derivative work to carry the attribution notices from the
original's NOTICE "excluding those notices that do not pertain to any part of the Derivative
Works", so they are excluded here rather than copied. Copying them would be worse than omitting
them: it would claim this site distributes an MPL-2.0 component and takes a position on model
weights, neither of which is true.

What carries over is the copyright attribution above.


WHAT THIS WEBSITE BUNDLES

Browser code, from npm, all permissively licensed. The authoritative list is `package-lock.json`;
these are the ones a reader would want named:

  Next.js, React, React DOM ...... MIT
  three.js ....................... MIT   (the landing page's WebGL scenes)
  @react-three/fiber, drei ....... MIT
  monaco-editor,
  @monaco-editor/react ........... MIT   (the read-only editor in the landing-page demo)
  clsx, tailwind-merge,
  class-variance-authority,
  tailwindcss-animate ............ MIT

None of these requires a notice beyond the copyright and permission text that accompanies it, which
is why they are listed rather than reproduced. Their full licence text is in `node_modules` in any
checkout and in the lockfile's resolved metadata.


THE LEGAL DOCUMENTS ARE NOT THIS PROJECT'S TO CHANGE HERE

`src/components/Legal/{PrivacyClient,TermsClient}.tsx` are copies of the desktop application's
Terms of Use and Privacy Policy. The original is the application's, because that is where a person
accepts them and where registration records which version was accepted. `npm run verify:legal`
refuses to build if this copy has drifted from the digest committed in `src/lib/legal.ts`.
